A||||6||BOILERMAKER||Interior color changes
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||06-21-99||07:49 AM||||I know that there is a special paint kit that is used to change the color of some of the interior items.  In my case I am wanting to change the gray to the brown color.  Can anybody help as to where I should look and what part number (if there is any) for finding such an item.<p>Thx
Z||000001||mwbackus||06-21-99||08:35 PM||||Dupli-color makes a spray paint product called "Vinyl and Fabric Color".  Autozone stocks this line of paint products.  I am not sure if they offer a color to match the brown interiors, but the black works great for faded speaker grills on a grey/blk formula interior.  Since the interior pieces are all basically the same, it would make more sense just to swap the pieces from another car (with brn interior).  The dash swap would present the biggest problem, but you would pratically have to remove it in order to paint it (with decent results) anyway.
Z||000002||PaUL||06-21-99||08:46 PM||||My advice to anyone contemplating changing the interior color with a spray on product is don't do it. A friend of mine tried this and his interior looked like crap afterwards. The paint has a tendency to flake and peel when applied to plastic or vinyl. The spray on color for fabrics works decent enough. I once used it to spray the entire carpet in a old car I wanted to sell. It looked ok and it covered up all the stains and dirt.
Z||000003||lowCG||06-22-99||12:04 AM||||I've used a product named Mar-Hyde before,a good product for vinyl and hard surfaces that lasts for years when used properly/prepped/cleaned.Only parts of my interior that showed any wear were the armrests on the doors,never chipped or flaked. <br>Stinks though,dries slow,so be prepared to wait a couple of days.<br>Makes sense to use something like this since that's the way GM did it(unfortunately).
Z||000004||burdell1||06-26-99||08:02 AM||||Where do you get that paint?<br>
Z||000005||lowCG||06-26-99||03:02 PM||||If you can't find it at a local car parts store,try asking at bodyshop supply stores.<br>Just got a car with a bite out of the lower edge of the dash,plan on filling with urethane caulk,and hopefully finding the GM gray in a Mar Hyde spray can.<br>Does anyone know of a product that will repair the skin on the foam door/window seals?
Z||000006||Carrolles||06-28-99||12:31 PM||||I have used a Vinyl and Plastic spray by S.E.M. that is an exact match for the light grey interior of my 85SE.  I got it at a local parts store but have also seen basic colors in WalMart.  I don't have the info with me.  I can look it up when I get home this weekend if you'd like.<p>Todd, do you have the info I e'mailed to you handy?<p>Regular spray paint won't stick to vinyl/plastic for long.<p>The S.E.M. can also be used on fabric but with a special application method.  Don't just spray it on heavily in one coat.  Spray a light misting coat over about a square foot of fabric then immediately brush it in with a nylon brush.  This prevents the spray from matting down the fabric.<p>Take care,<br>Carroll
